# Commits that moved code without changing it. `git blame` on this project is
# worth keeping usable — much of the value in the physics is in comments
# explaining where a constant came from, and a move would otherwise attribute
# every one of them to the refactor.
#
# Enable with:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# That on its own is not enough here, and it is worth knowing why. This code did
# not just get reformatted, it moved between files, and blame does not track
# content across files unless asked. Use:
#
#   git blame -C -C -C src/core/atmosphere.js
#
# With that, a physics comment resolves back to the commit that wrote it rather
# than to the move. Lines prettier also reflowed will still land on the format
# commit, because their text genuinely changed — only whole-line moves survive.
#
# Each of these left the design snapshot byte-identical, which is the evidence
# that they moved code rather than changed it.

